==English==

===Etymology===
{{der|en|gd|-}} {{compound|gd|Mac|Kenzie|t1=son of|t2=the intelligent one" or possibly "the wise ruler|nocat=1}} or “the bright one/the one born of fire”. Possible alternate: Gaelic {{m|und|MacCoinneach||Son of Kenneth}}. Originally a surname, the family motto being “I shine, not burn.”

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}
{{slim-wikipedia}}
{{wikipedia|Mackenzie River}}

# {{surname|en|from=Scottish Gaelic|dot=}} of [[Scottish]] origin.
# {{given name|en|female|from=surnames|usage=1970s and later}}, also in the form [[Makenzie]].
# {{given name|en|male}}.
# {{place|en|river|terr/Northwest Territories}}, the longest in [[Canada]], running from [[Great Slave Lake]] to the [[Beaufort Sea]].

